<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niccolò Tommaseo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1802">1802</a>–<a href="/years/1874">1874</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niccolò Tommaseo was an Italian writer and lexicographer, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, best known for his great dictionary of the Italian language. Imprisoned by the Austrians with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniele-manin">Daniele Manin</a> in January 1848, he was freed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> rose in March and served as a minister of the Republic of San Marco. After its fall in 1849 he went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niccolo-tommaseo.jpg" alt="Niccolò Tommaseo" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Egisto Sarri · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikola_Tommaseo_Tomasic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
